<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Motorola estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Motorola estimates raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said analyst Todd Koffman raised earnings per share estimates on Motorola Inc after the company posted better-than-expected second-quarter results.</p>
<p>-- boosted 1997 estimate to $2.71 from $2.58.</p>
<p>-- raised 1998 view to $3.65 from $3.40.</p>
<p>-- said in summary report Motorola was &quot;on the road to recovery.&quot;</p>
<p>-- excluding a charge, Motorola posted second quarter earnings of $0.62 a share.  The consensus estimate was $0.56, according to First Call.  The stock rose 3-1/8 to 85-5/8.</p>
</text>
